    {
      "@id": "http://smart.who.int/base/process/Process_SgEndToEnd",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/ns#Process",
      "name": "SMART Guideline end to end",
      "summary": "From a use case to a consuming application: identify the L1 guidelines, ingest them into an L1 knowledge graph, choose the L2 DAKs to build on, create or adapt the L2 assets, choose the L3 IGs to build on, produce the L3 assets, then build the L4 consuming ap…",
      "description": "From a use case to a consuming application: identify the L1 guidelines, ingest them into an L1 knowledge graph, choose the L2 DAKs to build on, create or adapt the L2 assets, choose the L3 IGs to build on, produce the L3 assets, then build the L4 consuming application the requester describes. Adjudication follows every stage as QA, not as a gate (owner, 2026-10-14: \"once agent produces L2 it can produce L3\"), but the order is a rule (owner, 2026-10-15: \"order strict, sign-off QA\"): no L3 asset before the L1 extraction and L2 assets it derives from exist with their review requested (Gateway_L3Ready). Each stage forks into the next stage and its adjudication, and each adjudication has its own end event, so the instance completes only when all are recorded. Each stage runs one named skill with its own input and output contract, named in brackets on the task (l2-dak-authoring.bpmn for stage 4, dak-l3-ig.bpmn for stage 6), and each stage's output is the next stage's input; the smart-guideline-end-to-end skill is the orchestrator that says so, and who adjudicates each.",
      "enforcement": "advisory",
      "sourcePath": "processes/content/smart-guideline-end-to-end.bpmn",
      "sourceUrl": "https://github.com/litlfred/smart-base/blob/main/smart-base/processes/content/smart-guideline-end-to-end.bpmn",
